.TH "GIT\-UNLOCK" "1" "December 2021" "" "Git Extras"
.SH "NAME"
\fBgit\-unlock\fR \- Unlock a file excluded from version control
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBgit unlock\fR <filename>
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Unmark a tracked local file with \fB\-\-no\-skip\-worktree\fR in the Git index so local modifications are tracked again by version control\. Requires a non\-empty <filename> argument referring to a tracked file\. If <filename> is omitted or empty, the command prints an error to stderr and exits with status 1\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
<filename>
.P
The name of the tracked file to unlock\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
$ git unlock config/database\.yml
.fi
